  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Framework Agreement with The Norwegian Center for Holocaust and Minority Studies</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Framework Agreement 2023-2025 with The Norwegian Center for Holocaust and Minority Studies (HL-senteret). The projects within the framework agreement aim to strengthen the work on religious and ethnic minorities. To achieve this, the projects will focus on developing knowledge, networks and competence among researchers, civil society actors and other practitioners who work to promote the rights of minorities. The projects focus in particular on the prevention of genocide and massive human rights violations, hate speech and group hostility, and the dissemination of research-based knowledge through online resources. A number of ODA-countries in the global south are targeted.

Project 1: The project is primarily thematic and comparative - linked to a number of ODA countries including, among others, Indonesia, the Philippines, Argentina, Columbia, Rwanda, Central African Republic, Sri Lanka, Myanmar and Iraq.
Project 2: Ukraine and the Balkans for a comparative perspective, but the emphasis is on South Africa.
Project 3: The ICHR project has Tunisia, Iraq, India, Rohingya refugees and to some extent Indonesia as the main case.</narrative>
  </description>
